  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You receive a **0-indexed** integer array `nums` of **even** length and there is also an empty array `arr`. Harper and Elijah decided to play a game where in every round Harper and Elijah will do one move. The rules of the game are as follows:\n\n* Every round, first Harper will remove the **smallest** element from `nums`, and then Elijah does the same.\n* Now, first Elijah will append the removed element in the array `arr`, and then Harper does the same.\n* The game continues until `nums` becomes empty.\n\nOutput *the resulting array* `arr`.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [5,4,2,3]\nOutput: [3,2,5,4]\nExplanation: In round one, first Harper removes 2 and then Elijah removes 3. Then in arr firstly Elijah appends 3 and then Harper appends 2. So arr = [3,2].\nAt the begining of round two, nums = [5,4]. Now, first Harper removes 4 and then Elijah removes 5. Then both append in arr which becomes [3,2,5,4].\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [2,5]\nOutput: [5,2]\nExplanation: In round one, first Harper removes 2 and then Elijah removes 5. Then in arr firstly Elijah appends and then Harper appends. So arr = [5,2].\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `2 <= nums.length <= 100`\n* `1 <= nums[i] <= 100`\n* `nums.length % 2 == 0`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
